deformMCMModule(...,DegreeLimit=>...) -- Compute only up to this exponent
*************************************************************************

Description
===========

This parameter is an integer $ n $ such that in the result of the computation
the versality criterion holds only after reducing the relevant rings modulo the
maximal homogeneous ideal to the power $ n+1 $. Concretely, this means that the
output may have incorrect terms with total exponent greater than $ n $. If the
input is positively graded, all deformation parameters have strictly positive
degree, and $ n $ is sufficiently large, then no terms of degree greater than $
n $ appear in the output, and the result is versal. In this case, the maximum
of $ d / deg x $ where $ d $ is the degree of the equation of the hypersurface
and $ x $ ranges over all variables in the ring of the hypersurface and all
deformation parameters, should suffice.

Functions with optional argument named DegreeLimit:
===================================================

  * "compose(Module,Module,Module,DegreeLimit=>...)" -- see *note compose:
    (Macaulay2Doc)compose, -- composition as a pairing on Hom-modules
  * *note deformMCMModule(...,DegreeLimit=>...):
    deformMCMModule_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegreeLimit=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, -- Compute only up
    to this exponent
  * "End(...,DegreeLimit=>...)" -- see *note End: (Macaulay2Doc)End, -- module
    of endomorphisms
  * "gb(...,DegreeLimit=>...)" -- see *note gb: (Macaulay2Doc)gb, -- compute a
    Gröbner basis
  * "Hom(...,DegreeLimit=>...)" -- see *note Hom: (Macaulay2Doc)Hom, -- module
    of homomorphisms
  * "homomorphism'(...,DegreeLimit=>...)" -- see *note homomorphism':
    (Macaulay2Doc)homomorphism', -- get the element of Hom from a homomorphism
  * "minimalBetti(...,DegreeLimit=>...)" -- see *note minimalBetti:
    (Macaulay2Doc)minimalBetti, -- minimal betti numbers of (the minimal free
    resolution of) a homogeneous ideal or module
  * normalCone(Ideal,DegreeLimit=>...) (missing documentation)
  * normalCone(Ideal,RingElement,DegreeLimit=>...) (missing documentation)
  * "pushForward(...,DegreeLimit=>...)" -- see *note
    pushForward(RingMap,Module):
    (Macaulay2Doc)pushForward_lpRingMap_cmModule_rp, -- compute the pushforward
    of a module along a ring map
  * quotient(...,DegreeLimit=>...) (missing documentation)
  * saturate(...,DegreeLimit=>...) (missing documentation)
  * "syz(...,DegreeLimit=>...)" -- see *note syz(Matrix):
    (Macaulay2Doc)syz_lpMatrix_rp, -- compute the syzygy matrix

Further information
===================

